   $q$Which statement best evaluates how well the structure makes the central idea clear?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is clear, because it tells the story of lichen research in the order discoveries were made.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"wrong-structure"},{"text":"It is unclear, because the examples of lichens as pioneers come before any explanation of what lichens are.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-sequence"},{"text":"It is unclear, because the final sentence introduces a claim that conflicts with the rest of the passage.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-conclusion"},{"text":"It is clear, because each section builds on the partnership named in paragraph 1: the partners, their exchange, and then its effects.","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is clear, because each section builds on the partnership named in paragraph 1: the partners, their exchange, and then its effects.$q$, $q$The passage names the partnership, explains each partner, condenses the exchange and then shows consequences, so every part supports the opening idea. The pioneer examples come after the explanation, not before, and the final sentence restates the partnership idea.$q$, 'draft', 'df66d435-30bc-5035-a2b4-bf514dabf824')
