values
  ('125dc58e-1b8c-5d95-a979-a3d9a424f55e', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'read-g11-text-structure'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The author names the "Magnus effect" only after explaining how the air moves around the ball. Which statement best evaluates this choice?$q$, $q$[{"text":"It is effective, because readers grasp the mechanism first, so the term attaches to an idea they already understand.","is_correct":true},{"text":"It shows that the name of the effect matters more than the process behind it.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misreads-purpose"},{"text":"It suggests the author doubts whether the Magnus effect is real.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"unsupported-inference"},{"text":"It is confusing, because readers cannot follow the process until they know its official name.","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"misjudges-effect"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$It is effective, because readers grasp the mechanism first, so the term attaches to an idea they already understand.$q$, $q$Explaining before labeling keeps the term from being unexplained jargon; by the time it appears, readers know what it means. The name is given with confidence, so nothing suggests doubt.$q$, 'draft', 'dd6e4043-1c3e-514b-aa63-9a0ad0b3b00d')
